 having at this point Gemma  just wants to shut the doll down  regardless of whatever excuses she makes  from here on out the climax of Megan is  basically one extended fight scene  though there's a lot of humor mixed in  with the action the same protective  Instinct that leads Megan to commit  violence also makes Megan wish to  protect her bonded primary from being  exposed to the same violence this leads  to a comical conundrum when Katie hears  the commotion and checks in to see  what's happening while she slams Gemma  against a table Megan claims that  they're not fighting Gemma goes along  with the ruse also to protect Katie but  don't come in here Katie it's kind of a  mess on gem is Right Katie I'm All Odds  and entering now but Katie isn't stupid  she soon not only fully aware of what's  happening but she also has to take sides  between the human Guardian she's been  assigned and the robot friend she's  cherished as the Fight Continues  throughout the house with Megan's  plastic face getting scarred in the  scuffle Gemma smartly points out that  there's no way Megan could kill her as  Megan's secondary user she should  theoretically be protected from Death  the Android acknowledges that her  Creator is correct but she doesn't plan  on killing Gemma in this fight anyway  instead Megan plans to turn one of the  tools of control Gemma has used against  her Megan is also designed for  palliative care Megan can keep Gemma  alive but just barely the blinking pen  device that was originally designed to  send override orders to Megan is  apparently also capable of being used as  a weapon to cause brain damage in humans  the doll threatens to use this weapon  against Gemma hurting her severely  enough that she'll never be able to  report any of the doll's crimes gemma's  only potential salvation at this moment  comes from Katie and another friend of  hers  seeing Megan attacking her aunt  definitely snaps Katie out of her  unnatural emotional attachment to the  machi