uce for the  first time Katie was curious how her  aunt designed Bruce so Gemma removed the  plate covering the robot's faceless head  showing off its inner workings she  pointed out the cameras used for eyes a  sensor to give it a sense of smell and  the most important detail for the end of  the film a single processing chip at the  bottom of the face that serves as the  robot's brain gemma's skill at robotics  has continued to progress beyond that  early creation but she was still using  some of the same design principles when  she was designing Megan open up the  robot doll space and the insides of its  head look much the same as the insides  of Bruce's including a brain chip in the  same location as Gemma wrestles on the  ground with an overpowering Megan she  manages to open up the robot's face  providing an opening for Katie to stab  the chip permanently deactivating what  remains of the doll's body  horror movie Monsters only tend to stay  dead until a sequel rolls around in the  case of Megan the Production Studio  blumhouse and co-creator slash producer  James 1 have plenty of experience in  building a long-lasting franchise I get  accused of being the master of killer  doll movies with that in mind it makes  sense that the final moments of Megan  introduce a logical explanation for how  the killer artificial intelligence can  return in future films as Gemma and  Katie walk outside the house in the  film's closing scene the camera stays  inside focused on the tiny robot control  center of the House's smart home  assistant right before the cut credits  the machine turns on and starts moving  on its own the clear implication is that  Megan's intelligence has escaped onto  the internet or at least to other  devices also for a potential sequel hook  there's the not quite fully addressed  matter of the competing toy companies  that might still want to make their own  equivalents to Megan we don't know for  sure if the stolen data files added  ended up getting seen by anyone else so  the code could very well end up in the  wrong hands if one Megan is scary enough  imagine a sequel where these killer  dolls get mass produced  [Music]
 

